WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.236 line:0%
-Welcome to the show.
It is nice to meet you.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.570 line:0%
Thank you so much for coming on.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.806 line:0%
-Thank you for having me.
I've always wanted to do this.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.008 line:0%
-Yeah.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.510
Yeah. Wow.
You did it right there.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.044
Yeah, you -- That's it.

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:13.846
Thank you for
coming to New York.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.615
I know you're probably coming
from L.A. or Australia.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:18.051
-L.A.
-L.A., yeah.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.952
Have you spent much time
in New York?

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.287
-I've spent a little bit
of time here.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.956
I try to come sort of
as often as possible

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.392
to see the plays
that are on and everything.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:30.230
But my parents are here,
and one of the biggest memories

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.598
I have coming here
was when I was younger.

00:00:32.598 --> 00:00:33.833
And I came with them.
So this is one of my first --

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:34.967
-Where is your mom?

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.335
-I'm trying to find them
while I'm speaking.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:37.803
-Oh, hey, there they are.
I see them.

00:00:37.803 --> 00:00:39.339
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:42.175
-Hi, mom. Hi, dad.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.276
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:45.879
Yeah, it's also
their first time.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.179
-Yes.

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:48.881
-It's their first time
being on "The Tonight Show,"

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.349
as well, which is perfect.

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:51.651
-We're in it together.

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:54.254
-When did you come to
the city with your parents?

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.122
-I think I was 8 years old.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.724
And we sort of did all the
stuff, like all the sights.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.762
And I remember my dad sort of
surprised me with tickets

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.998
to a Knicks game, because I was
a big basketball fan.

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:06.166
-Oh, yeah, and where did --

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.033
-Yeah, we were in
the nosebleeds, up the back,

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.403
but I remember it was just,
like -- It was, like --

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.071
It was the most special
experience, though.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.472
You know what I mean?

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.274
-Don't you have some news
to tell your parents?

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:18.745
-Yeah. We're going to the Knicks
tomorrow, but way closer.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.514
[ Applause ]

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:25.351
-Yeah, that's right. Way closer.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.786
-Yeah.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.789
-Now, the new season
of "Euphoria"

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:33.525
had a giant premiere on Sunday.

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:34.727
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.896
-It's become a huge, huge hit.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.399
Did you have any idea
that it would be this big

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.233
the second time around,
the second season?

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:44.103
-No, I didn't know, and then
they told me this morning

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.073
that it, like,
crashed the website.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.276
And, you know, a lot of people
have seen it, so it's -- Yeah.

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.912
It's so scary.
-I'll tell you what's scary.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.148
You're getting your own
wax figure at Madame Tussauds.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.649
-Yeah.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:02:01.954
-Now, I'm lucky enough to be --
I've done it myself, as well.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.155
Have you been through
the whole process yet?

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:04.424
-I did.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:05.991
I went through the process,
and it was strange,

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:09.262
but the strangest thing is their
shirts that the crew wear

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:13.800
say like, "Paparazzi"
and like, "Celebrity."

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.501
That was the
strangest thing for me.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.337
Like, you've got all these
cameras in front of you

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.871
and you've got all these
little dots on your face.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:22.141
It looks like behind the scenes
of "Planet of the Apes."

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.776
And then these people
in shirts that say like

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.144
"Paparazzi"
and like, "Celebrity."

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.246
-Really? I didn't see that...
-Yeah, it was peculiar.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:30.783
-...on mine.
-Great people.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.986
-I don't know if you have
legit people doing it.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:37.323
-It's like a gang of paparazzi
just, like, lured me in --

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.724
-Taking your picture, yeah.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:41.193
It turns out your
wax figure is this big.

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:44.430
-Yeah, it's a bobblehead.
-It's LEGOs. Yeah, exactly.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.265
This show, "Euphoria,"
I will say,

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.501
is pretty dark at some parts,

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.536
pretty, you know --

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.106
It must be stressful
to do a show like this.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.308
But I heard that
to keep it loose,

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.976
you would do you this thing
where you would grab

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.178
people's phones and just take
selfies with their phones?

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.213
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:03.148
-Now, how do you go with that --
I like the bit,

00:03:03.148 --> 00:03:04.417
but what is it?

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:05.818
-Well, it's not even, like,
"Euphoria"-specific.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:09.055
I think was in New York a couple
of weeks ago and I was at a bar,

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.591
and someone had left their phone
sort of on a table somewhere.

00:03:12.591 --> 00:03:14.026
And I kind of just, like --
There's something about it.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.361
Like, I want them to find it.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.662
I have this idea
that they're going to have

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:18.697
the phone for like 40 years,
and in 40 years' time,

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:19.832
they're going to be like,

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.401
"Oh, I'm going to go through
my camera roll,"

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.001
like they don't
go through it every day,

00:03:23.001 --> 00:03:24.670
and be like, "Oh, my God.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.407
Who is this?"

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.474
-No, they know who you are.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.276
But you just grab
a phone and just --

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:31.878
-Yeah, like,
but I don't move it,

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.812
because I don't
want to be invasive.

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:37.417
So I do the slide up.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:39.686
-Oh, that's very nice of you.
I appreciate that.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.154
Yeah, thoughtful.
-Yeah, like a pigeon.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:45.358
-Yeah, very thoughtful of you
to do that, yeah.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.561
In this show,
you play Nate, who --

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.930
He's not really a good guy.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.531
No.

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:55.301
But at the end of
Sunday's episode,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.870
your character is
a little changed kind of.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:58.905
Well --
-Yeah.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.741
-He gets beat up.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.710
-But fans were like,
"Well, he had it coming."

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.079
-Yeah, they were stoked.
They were so happy about it.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.814
-And would you agree with that?

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:11.450
-Well...

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:12.751
-I mean, it is you.

00:04:12.751 --> 00:04:16.289
-I think me as Jacob,
I would love to beat him up.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.291
Like, I would love to give him
a clip around the ears.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.095
But as Nate, you know,
I feel very bad for him.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.163
-Yeah, because you are
his character.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.164
You're playing
the character so well.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.599
-Yeah, I had to get beat up.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:27.599
-Yeah, and you don't want to get
beat up, but --

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:29.435
-It sucked.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:31.103 line:0%
-You look fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.171 line:0%
-Thank you for coming
on to the show.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.505 line:0%
I appreciate this.

00:04:33.505 --> 00:04:36.708 line:0%
I think the last time I saw you,
you were with your dad.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.010 line:0%
Your dad was on our show.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:41.180 line:0%
-Yes, and that was a very
embarrassing day for me.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.682
-Why was that embarrassing?

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:45.752
-Well, I had just gotten off
the flight to see my dad

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.920
and I came here and I,
like, looked disgusting.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.422
And I was just, kind of hiding
in the dressing room,

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:52.725
and my dad's friend was like,
"Oh, do you want to go upstairs

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:54.793
and, like, check out
the 'SNL' floor?"

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:56.361
And I was like, "Sure.

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:58.497
Like, hope I don't run into
anyone, whatever."

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.300
Harry Styles was hosting,
and I knew that, but I --

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.003
I was like, "There's no way
I'm going to see him, right?"

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.706
And then, the first thing --

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.741
Like, I walked into the room,
and he was right there.

00:05:09.741 --> 00:05:12.611
And I literally,
like, could not --

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:13.846
Like, I went into shock.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.915
Like, I didn't even know
what to do with myself.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.650
And then I --
Yeah, I just went into a panic

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.652
and then I got back down
to the dressing room

00:05:20.652 --> 00:05:23.822
and started hysterically crying

00:05:23.822 --> 00:05:26.926
because I was so overwhelmed
and just not expecting that.

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:29.929
And then you
knocked on the door.

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.031
And I was so humiliated
and I hear like,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.265
"Hey, Judd, it's Jimmy."

00:05:33.265 --> 00:05:35.367
And I was like,
"Oh, no, no, no!"

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:40.506
And then I -- Yeah, so, then I
just turned and faced the wall,

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.109
like, thinking, like,
maybe if I turn around,

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.078
you won't notice I was there.

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:47.746
But the room was really small.
-Yeah.

00:05:47.746 --> 00:05:51.017
-So, yeah, and then
you saw that I was crying.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.953
And I was really humiliated by
that for like -- And I still am.

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.821
Like, telling it, I'm like,
"Why am I telling this?"

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:58.290
-Oh, no, I didn't -- That's
normally the reaction I get

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.759
when I say hi
to people backstage.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.662
You weren't crying tonight,
I will say that.

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:05.197
Backstage, you were not crying.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.999
But why were you nervous
for Harry?

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:09.602
Just -- Didn't you interview him
or interview One Direction?

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:13.806
-Yeah, I did interview
One Direction when I was 14.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.375
-Now, what was this -- How did
you get a chance to do that?

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.711
-I don't even --
I had a popular Twitter page

00:06:19.711 --> 00:06:21.847
when I was like 13.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:25.284
-And I decided I wanted
to become a child journalist,

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.786
and they asked me
to interview One Direction

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:30.055
on their first trip to America.

00:06:30.055 --> 00:06:33.459
-Wow! And so, that must be
nerve-racking.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.995
-Yeah, it was, like,
the scariest thing in my life.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:39.565
-Yeah, and I know that you were
freaking out before you --

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.367
right before you were
going to interview them.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:46.439
And you were -- You were upset,
but your dad videotaped you.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.706
-Yeah.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:49.609
-Well, we talked to your dad.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:51.910
And we have a video.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.213
If you don't mind us
showing this,

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:55.948
this is 14-year-old Maude Apatow

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:58.484
preparing to interview
One Direction.

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.086
Here we go.
-Ooh!

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.754
-In 10 minutes, you'll be
in the room with One Direction.

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.055
Let's go!
-[ Shouting indistinctly ]

00:07:03.755 --> 00:07:06.426
[ Laughing, wheezing ]

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.964
-What is that?

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.100
-I couldn't even say words.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.102
Like, they're just --
They weren't coming out.

00:07:17.102 --> 00:07:18.804
-We have a picture of you, too,

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.873
minutes before
you were interviewing them.

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.909
Look at you.
You're so emotional.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.643
I mean...

00:07:24.643 --> 00:07:27.713
[ Cymbal crash ]
Oh, my gosh.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.115
Yeah, that was you.

00:07:30.115 --> 00:07:32.451
But then this is you actually
interviewing the boys,

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.153
and you did a great job.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:36.855
-I don't know if I did
such a great job, honestly.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:38.457
-Oh, really? Was it bad?

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:41.760
-I don't think--
It couldn't have been good.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.762
-Would you ever listen to it
again or play it back?

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:44.797
-No.
-No, of course not.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:47.332
No, no, no.
-God no. No, no, no.

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:48.967
-Well, shortly after that,

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:52.437
you got to see One Direction
in concert.

00:07:52.437 --> 00:07:54.073
Your dad told us this.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.809
-I did, yes.
-And that must have been fun.

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:59.645
It probably went -- You probably
weren't nervous then?

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.947
-No. It was worse then.

00:08:01.947 --> 00:08:08.287
-So, we have a video of you
right after the concert.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:09.455
[ Laughing ]

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.823
So, you saw the concert.
You had a great time.

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:11.824
-Yeah.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:13.191
-And then,
this is after the concert

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:15.094
with your family
and your sister.

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:17.596
And here's -- Yeah, take a look.

00:08:17.596 --> 00:08:19.632
-[ Sobbing ]

00:08:24.036 --> 00:08:26.506
-Maude, you're fine.

00:08:29.708 --> 00:08:32.011
-"Maude, you're fine."

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:33.879
-Oh, my God.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:37.850
-You have good parents
to send that video to us,

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.853
so thank you to --
We appreciate that.

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:43.155
How is the family?
Everyone good?

00:08:43.155 --> 00:08:44.857
-Yeah, everyone's great.
-Alright. We're fans.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.759
Please say hi
to everyone over there.

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.394
I want to talk about "Euphoria."

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.730
This is a...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:56.368
...massive, massive, massive hit
on HBO this season.

00:08:56.368 --> 00:08:59.038
Bigger than anything
in the world.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:00.272
And everyone was
talking about it, like,

00:09:00.272 --> 00:09:03.175
broke ratings records,
all this stuff.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:06.244
But it's more finding
the backstories

00:09:06.244 --> 00:09:08.380
of a lot of
the characters on this one.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.984
Now, what can we expect for your
character, for Lexi?

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:15.621
-I think you'll see a lot more
of my character this season.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.223
I don't know if
I can even say anything.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.490
I'm going to get in trouble.
-Yeah, I know.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.192
-But it's all exciting,

00:09:20.192 --> 00:09:22.561
and I think people
are going to be surprised.

00:09:22.561 --> 00:09:25.597
I think, like, people think
my character is sort of

00:09:25.597 --> 00:09:28.467
this shy, like, sweet one,
but I think she might be

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:30.603
just as crazy as everyone else.

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:32.905
-Oh, my gosh. No, you're --

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:35.908
-No, she's not.
-Alright.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.543
I don't know
if I can handle that.

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:38.777
You were telling me,
though, backstage

00:09:38.777 --> 00:09:40.745
that every shot is
very technical on that show.

00:09:40.745 --> 00:09:42.014
-It is very technical.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:45.651
So, they'll, like,
do these long shots

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:49.021
where they don't make any edits,
so they'll have us, like,

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.489
walking through
the school hallways,

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:53.358
and it will be like
two minutes without any cuts.

00:09:53.358 --> 00:09:57.196
So if you mess up,
the whole shot is destroyed,

00:09:57.196 --> 00:09:59.865
and I always mess it up.

00:09:59.865 --> 00:10:01.233
So then, yeah, basically --

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.603
-So if you mess up,
everyone has to redo the --

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.637
-And it became,
like, a running joke

00:10:05.637 --> 00:10:07.539
that I would always
miss my mark.

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:08.974
Because they put,
like, a tiny, little piece

00:10:08.974 --> 00:10:10.342
of tape on the ground.

00:10:10.342 --> 00:10:11.543
And you can't look at it,

00:10:11.543 --> 00:10:12.945
because then it's obvious
you're trying to find it.

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:14.246
-Yeah, that is true.

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:16.147
So you just have to,
like, zone and find the mark,

00:10:16.147 --> 00:10:17.983
and you'll be like -- So,
they'll do the tracking shot,

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:19.852
and then you got to be like...

00:10:19.852 --> 00:10:20.886
"Hey --" You know, whatever.

00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:21.887
-Exactly!

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:22.888
-And they're like,
"No, over here."

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:23.989
And you go, "Oh, yeah."
"Hey!"

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:25.724
-I'm always like
10 inches off of the mark.

00:10:25.724 --> 00:10:27.125
-Just a little bit off.

00:10:27.125 --> 00:10:29.127
-But then they were like --
They started putting, like,

00:10:29.127 --> 00:10:33.332
sandbags and boxes so I would
just, like, knock into it.

00:10:33.332 --> 00:10:35.534
-You have to walk into a wall
to hit your mark?

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.704
-Yeah, it still didn't work.

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:42.474
-Yeah, I had one line
in "Band of Brothers,"

00:10:42.474 --> 00:10:44.343
this miniseries on HBO.

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.245
And Tom Hanks was directing.

00:10:46.245 --> 00:10:48.847
And I had to drive
a World War II Jeep

00:10:48.847 --> 00:10:50.182
and then say like, "Hey, boys,

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:51.783
I'm getting the ammo"
or something.

00:10:51.783 --> 00:10:53.085
And I go, "Great, let's do it."

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:54.520
And they go, "Oh, we got to wait
for it be nighttime."

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:55.988
I go, "Nighttime?"

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.589
And then he goes,
"We got to get the extras."

00:10:57.589 --> 00:10:59.224
And they had 200 extras.

00:10:59.224 --> 00:11:01.994
I had to drive through
all these soldiers

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:05.564
trying to find my mark, where
I'm driving a car to my mark

00:11:05.564 --> 00:11:07.366
and then say,
"I'm bringing ammo."

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:10.069
And I was maybe
like a mile off the mark.

00:11:10.069 --> 00:11:12.004
So I drove in
and then just parked.

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.240
I go, "We got ammo, boys!
We got it."

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:16.074
And then Tom was way over there.

00:11:16.074 --> 00:11:17.909
I was like,
"Where is everybody?"

00:11:17.909 --> 00:11:20.045
He was like, "Dude,
you're way off the mark, buddy.

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:23.115
Can we replace him right now?
He's so bad."

00:11:23.115 --> 00:11:24.783
But you were phenomenal in this,

00:11:24.783 --> 00:11:27.053
and everyone is buzzing
and talking about you.

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:29.255
Congratulations
on all the success.

